pub const AGENTS_NOTE : str = "docs/agents/AGENTS_ALPHABET.md \"Who holds a tool, and who holds a skill\" binds every tool to the Queen (T). Domain lead C, V: CHANGED (V,C -> C,V): the lead was on V, but vsim.rs says outright \"It reports and never gates\" and refuses to judge, which is not a verdict tool; its subject is the Verilog backend's output -- ABOUT \"How far each spec gets when its generated Verilog is actually RUN\" -- and every defect the module doc credits it with (a float multiply routed through an integer ladder, `break` lowered to `disable fork`, an early `return` that does not leave its loop, `invariant` emitted as a comment) is a lowering bug, so C leads and V stays second as the simulating arm \"that can catch a defect whose whole nature is that it compiles\".";
; From the about text (long about when the doc has more than one paragraph); no marketing.
